/-!
# Full matrix algebra for the 45-dimensional dual induced factor

The saved polynomial is evaluated by grouped, checked Horner steps. Its value is the
outer product of the first column and row orbit vectors. Checked predecessor
recurrences and right inverses prove both orbits span the whole space.

All matrices here are literal certificates for `factorMatrix 0`. Source context:
Guralnick–Malle, Classification of 2F-modules I, Proposition 5.1, pp.15–16,
and Theorem 6.6/Table 6.7. See `../source/README.md` for original attribution.
Generated by `source/generate.py`; numerical identities use `decide +kernel`.
-/

